-- title:
--   Globalising a locally ideal-cut condition on ring maps
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring (in a fixed universe), and let $P$ assign to every commutative ring $A'$ in that universe and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : A \to A'$ a proposition. Assume: (i) $P$ is stable under post-composition, i.e. $P(A',\varphi)$ implies $P(A'',\chi \circ \varphi)$ for every ring homomorphism $\chi : A' \to A''$; (ii) $P$ is Zariski-local on the target, i.e. whenever $s : \kappa \to A'$ is a family whose range spans the unit ideal of $A'$ and $P$ holds for the composite of $\varphi$ with the localisation map $A' \to A'[1/s_k]$ for every $k$, then $P(A',\varphi)$ holds. Assume further given an index type $\kappa$, a family $r : \kappa \to A$ whose range spans the unit ideal of $A$, and for each $i$ an ideal $K_i$ of the localisation $A[1/r_i]$, such that for every $i$, every commutative ring $A'$ and every ring homomorphism $\chi : A[1/r_i] \to A'$ one has $P(A', \chi \circ \lambda_i) \iff \mathrm{map}_{\chi}(K_i) = 0$, where $\lambda_i : A \to A[1/r_i]$ is the structure map and $\mathrm{map}_\chi$ denotes the ideal of $A'$ generated by the image. The conclusion is that there exists a single ideal $I$ of $A$ with $P(A',\varphi) \iff \mathrm{map}_{\varphi}(I) = 0$ for every commutative ring $A'$ and every $\varphi : A \to A'$.
--
--   This is the affine form of the descent of ideals (quasi-coherence of ideal sheaves) along a cover of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ by basic open sets: a functorial, target-local condition on ring maps out of $A$ which is cut out by an ideal after each of the localisations $A[1/r_i]$ is cut out by one ideal of $A$ globally. It is used in the construction of the closed subscheme representing such a condition, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_factors_iff_of_idealCut`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isClosedImmersion_forall_factors_iff_of_idealCut).
-- source:
